.Dd June 23, 2026
.Dt CC-BURN 1
.Os zdots
.Sh NAME
.Nm cc-burn
.Nd Claude Code token burn-rate and 5h-window monitor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -json | Fl -quiet | Cm calibrate | Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
wraps
.Xr ccusage 1
(local, offline \(em reads
.Pa ~/.claude
transcripts, no network) and reports burn rate, time-to-reset for the rolling
5-hour usage window, projected end-of-window usage, cache reuse, and threshold
severity against a self-calibrating ceiling.
.Pp
.Sy Self-calibration :
the ceiling defaults to the maximum of your own completed 5h windows and rises
as you go, so the percentage means "% of your heaviest-ever window" and converges
toward the real plan limit the first time you hit a throttle. Pin a fixed ceiling
with
.Ev ZDOTS_CC_WINDOW_BUDGET .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width calibrate
.It (default)
Human-readable report.
.It Fl -json
Active block plus computed fields \(em consumed by
.Xr cc-burn-watch 8 ,
the ccusage MCP, and the status line.
.It Fl -quiet
One compact line for the status line.
.It Cm calibrate
Show the self-calibrated ceiling and the window history it is derived from.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 normal; 2 at or over the alert percentage for the current window; 3 if
.Xr ccusage 1
is unavailable.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ZDOTS_CC_WINDOW_BUDGET
.It Ev ZDOTS_CC_WINDOW_BUDGET
Pin a fixed ceiling in tokens (default
.Dq max ,
i.e. auto-calibrate). Find your plan ceiling with Claude Code's
.Ic /usage .
.It Ev ZDOTS_CC_WARN_PCT
Warn at this percent of the ceiling (default 70).
.It Ev ZDOTS_CC_ALERT_PCT
Alert at this percent of the ceiling (default 90).
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cc-burn-watch 8 ,
.Xr cc-doctor 1
.Pp
Surfaced live on the zdots.local console.
